{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1484761-have-arm-wrack-irl","id":1484761,"title":"Have Arm wrack irl","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-06-23T01:42:14-07:00","id":1484761,"title":"Have Arm wrack irl","content":"broke my arm in my own apartment the tilt as written does not do the condition justice<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The actual break was almost painless but trying to move after it was anything but","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-23T08:38:37-07:00","id":1484778,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1484761-have-arm-wrack-irl#post1484761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">broke my arm in my own apartment the tilt as written does not do the condition justice<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The actual break was almost painless but trying to move after it was anything but</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, one, I'm sorry to hear that, I hope you recover quickly.<br /> <br /> Two, I suppose we can use this to reiterate a thing about Chronicles that doesn't come up often but has been acknowledged even by the writers before-PC's, and people in general, are actually kind of better overall than most actual people, in terms of their capacity.<br /> <br /> Years ago, when White Wolf still had a web magazine, they had an article about Speed in games and how that was a regular thing that could actually be tested for, so they got everyone together to do a sprint based on the numbers they provided (the average human operating on 2 dots up and down the board, so speed was Strength 2 + Dexterity 2 + Size 5, resulting in Speed 9, which was translated into nine yards in three seconds), and found that a lot of people, unsurprisingly, couldn't actually make that spring (nevermind making a double move in that time). So part of the conclusion from that is that PCs and people in general are just tougher in the Chronicles universe than you'd expect. Being able to handle an Arm wrack (which isn't always a broken arm but can definitely include it) as they do is another example of that.<br /> <br /> If you wanted to do a thematic read of that, it also leans into the games general humanism and belief in people-it's the idea that most people are actually tougher than we'd give them credit for, that when the chips are down, people can surprise you in how they step up.<br /> <br /> Also the importance of those Medicine rolls. Again, I hope you recover quickly!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-23T13:09:48-07:00","id":1484799,"title":"","content":"As someone that has broken a bone in the middle of a sparring match before:<br /> <br /> There's a reason why the same separates Tilts and Conditions. Tilts take place in the time frame of seconds. While your adrenaline is bumping, your brain is in survival mode, and all sorts of things are pushing you to not really appreciate the damage you're dealing with. Conditions is what comes after (this is a thing in the books, Tilts don't last past combat, but can become a Condition if appropriate), and a Condition can be more easily fine tuned to the real impacts of a break.<br /> <br /> Though it's also just a game, abstractions are never going to fully capture these things. The CofD was, as directly stated by the 1e developers, more generous than realistic about recovering from injuries because a character being laid up for a few months while a bone heals isn't really fun &quot;play&quot; for the game. Less severe than reality penalties for dealing with a broken bone means you can play while healing. Otherwise most people are going to time-skip past it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-10T14:51:44-07:00","id":1489683,"title":"","content":"I had an obvious deformity of my arm at first it was corrected the day after the fall by surrgery ideas how to stat that up?<br /> <br /> or slings braces etc","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-10T16:40:06-07:00","id":1489688,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted 